import EnLayout from "../../layouts/EnLayout.astro";
---
<EnLayout
  title="Editorial policy"
  description="How Fortelese English editions are researched, written, corrected and updated — including our limits and what we refuse to publish."
>
  <p class="eyebrow">Trust</p>
  <h1>Editorial policy</h1>
  <div class="prose">
    <h2>What we publish</h2>
    <p>Long-form explainers that help a reader make a decision: how a product or market works, what it costs, what questions to ask, and where the traps are. We publish in English under the Fortelese English edition and in Arabic on the root site. The two editions are kept separate: no article is published in both languages under one URL.</p>

    <h2>What we refuse to publish</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Invented statistics, rankings or prices. If we quote a figure, the source is named or the figure is described as an example calculation.</li>
      <li>Paid placement presented as editorial. No provider pays for a recommendation here.</li>
      <li>Medical, legal or investment advice presented as personal guidance.</li>
      <li>Content copied from another publisher without attribution.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How an article is produced</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>A question a reader actually asks is chosen, not a keyword alone.</li>
      <li>The structure follows the decision: what it is, what to compare, what to ask, what to avoid.</li>
      <li>Every numeric example is a calculation we show, not a claim about the market.</li>
      <li>Financial and insurance articles carry an explicit disclaimer about their educational scope.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>Corrections</h2>
    <p>If you find an error, write to us with the page URL and the exact sentence. We review, correct, and record the update date on the page. Substantive corrections are made in the article itself, not in a comment hidden elsewhere.</p>

    <h2>Dates</h2>
    <p>Each article shows its publication date. Where an article is updated, the update date is shown alongside it. Articles imported from earlier editions keep their original publication date.</p>

    <h2>Language separation</h2>
    <p>The English edition lives under <code>/en/</code> and carries English metadata, English navigation and English feeds. The Arabic edition lives on the root and is Arabic throughout. Subdomains from earlier versions of this site redirect to the correct edition, never to a mixed-language page.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Editorial and correction requests: <a href="mailto:admin1@fortelese.com">admin1@fortelese.com</a></p>
  </div>
</EnLayout>
